rence\",\n      \"explanation\": \"A notable characteristic of copper cabling, as opposed to fiber optics, is its susceptibility to electromagnetic interference. \\\"CABOS DE COBRE\\\" (Copper Cables) are described as more prone to interference when compared to fiber optic cables [Data: Entities (488)]. This inherent limitation is also reflected in the description of \\\"TOMADA RJ (RJ45/RJ11)\\\", which states that while used for data and telephony, they are limited in speed and distance compared to fiber optics and susceptible to electromagnetic interference [Data: Entities (2531)]. This characteristic is important when considering the deployment of copper-based networks in environments with high electromagnetic noise, potentially impacting performance and reliability, especially for high-speed applications.\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"rating\": 6.0,\n  \"rating_explanation\": \"The impact severity is rated as moderate due to the fundamental role of these cabling standards in modern communication infrastructure and the potential for performance limitations and interference.\"\n}", "refusal": null, "role": "assistant", "annotations": null, "audio": null, "function_call": null, "tool_calls": null, "provider_specific_fields": {"refusal": null, "reasoning": null}}, "provider_specific_fields": {"native_finish_reason": "STOP"}}], "created": 1787751050, "model": "google/gemini-2.5-flash-lite", "object": "chat.completion", "moderation": null, "service_tier": "default", "system_fingerprint": null, "usage": {"completion_tokens": 1571, "prompt_tokens": 3813, "total_tokens": 5384, "completion_tokens_details": {"accepted_prediction_tokens": null, "audio_tokens": 0, "reasoning_tokens": 0, "rejected_prediction_tokens": null, "image_tokens": 0}, "prompt_tokens_details": {"audio_tokens": 0, "cache_write_tokens": 0, "cached_tokens": 0, "video_tokens": 0}, "cost": 0.0010097, "is_byok": false, "cost_details": {"upstream_inference_cost": 0.0010097, "upstream_inference_prompt_cost": 0.0003813, 